"""Huma Control Center — performance, fan, keyboard backlight and power settings for the Monster Huma H4.

Hardware is read through the qc71_laptop driver (huma-control/driver). Writes that
need root go through pkexec to the huma-control-helper and huma-control-power helpers
(polkit rules don't ask for a password). The keyboard backlight is driven via UPower;
turning it off when idle and starting it off in daytime is handled by the
huma-control-keyboard system service (settings in /etc/huma-control/keyboard.json).

Reading the driver files goes to the embedded controller (EC) over WMI, so hardware
reads happen in the background and the UI only shows the results.
"""
